{
  "about": "Two Thin Coats (Duncan Rhodes Painting Academy, Trans Atlantis Games): the triads of its three waves. A triad is the maker's set of three tones of one colour: a shadow, a midtone and a highlight. An input of scripts/build-dataset.mjs: each paint of a triad gets `family` and `tone` (docs/TONE_LADDERS.md §6).",
  "source": {
    "publisher": "Duncan Rhodes Painting Academy / Trans Atlantis Games",
    "url": "https://duncanrhodes.com/ttc-paints/",
    "charts": {
      "Wave 1, Paint Reference Chart (2022)": "https://www.duncanrhodes.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Colour-Wheel-Wave-1_2023_01.pdf",
      "Wave 1, Paint Conversion Chart (2022)": "https://www.duncanrhodes.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Conversion-Chart-Wave-1_2023_01.pdf",
      "Wave 2, Paint Reference Chart (2023)": "https://www.duncanrhodes.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Colour-Wheel-Wave-2_2023_01.pdf",
      "Wave 2, Paint Conversion Chart (2023)": "https://www.duncanrhodes.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Conversion-Chart-Wave-2_2023_01.pdf",
      "Wave 3, Paint Comparison Chart (2024)": "https://www.duncanrhodes.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Wave-3-Colour-Chart_2024.pdf"
    },
    "captured": "2026-11-18",
    "method": "The maker's page says: \"We have designed these, including most of the the metallics, as a triad system. That means we start off with your Shadow colour, then your Mid-tone and finally your Highlight.\" Its charts are images with no text, so they were read by eye. Each paint on a chart has a mark from the \"Paint bottle key\": S (shadow), M (midtone), H (highlight), W (wash), ME (metallic), G (glaze), B (brights) or E (effect). Waves 1 and 2: the Paint Reference Chart shows each triad (a part of the wheel, or three paints under a heading), and the Paint Conversion Chart, a second chart, has the same paints in the same sets of S, M, H. Wave 3 has one chart only: its paints are in rows of S, M, H, S, M, H, and each run of S, M, H is taken as a triad. No colour value was taken.",
    "order": "In each triad the paints are the shadow, the midtone and the highlight, in that order: tones 1, 2 and 3.",
    "rule": "A triad is a family when its three paints have the marks S, M and H. The sets with other marks are not tones of one colour and are not here: the washes (W), the Wave 2 and Wave 3 metallics (ME), the glazes (G), the brights (B) and the varnishes (E). The maker gives the place of each paint, so the build does not test the order against the app's approximate colour values. In two triads those values do not rise from dark to light (see lightness).",
    "heading": "`heading` is the maker's own word for a triad, where the chart has one (\"Warm Brown\"). The triads on the wheels and all Wave 3 triads have no heading, so the family has no name. Two Wave 2 triads are under one heading, \"Flesh Tones\".",
    "names": "`paints` has the names as they are in the app's data after the build's corrections. Five names of these paints were wrong in the community source and now have the charts' spelling: Skeleton Legion (was Keleton Legion), Emerald Green (Merald Green), Fur Cloak (Ur Cloak), Eldar Robe (Elder Robe), Von Evile Purple (Von Evile Pimple). One name on the Wave 3 chart is an evident printing error, \"Enticing Puple\": the data keeps \"Enticing Purple\".",
    "lightness": {
      "about": "Triads whose colour values in the app (from the community source) fall by more than 3 L* from one tone to the next. The maker's order is kept. The values of metallic paints are the least sure in the data (docs/COLOUR_CHECK.md).",
